    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai, mini.operators\n\n### Description\n\nMini.ai currently has a [hardcoded check](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/801627023acf3c41293ac321a43de009076ba037/lua/mini/ai.lua#L991C1-L992C1) to allow `d` and `c` to be used in an empty region.\r\n\r\nOther operators (like `gr` from mini.operators) also make sense to be used in an emtpy region, so it would be nice to be able to have a configuration option for this.",
