        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I didn't opt-in for new config setting, but instead decided to specifically hand pick \"replace\" from 'mini.operators' to allow acting on empty region.\r\n\r\nThe reason for this decision is slightly technical. Basically, Neovim doesn't really allow empty selections. But as it is useful to do `ci)`/`di)`/`gri)` for empty brackets, there is a [hack](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f32ac0a2a47298b768b6041fba30eeaabec338ba/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1018-L1026) which convert empty selection into one space selection. This means that only operators guaranteed to not essentially use selection can be acted on empty selection. From built-in those are `c` and `d` (although they do cut that text in default register). \"Replace\" from 'mini.operators' is another example. I don't think there is something else worth adding to this hand picked \"allow list\".\r\n\r\nAll that said, thanks again for suggestion! Being able to `gri)` for empty brackets is indeed quite useful.",
